=== NEW FINDING D-031-2 (guard strength, logged NOT implemented per FREEZE) ===
check-invariants.sh guard #7a
(`grep -qE 'geometry::is_touchbar_digitizer' src/providers/input.rs`)
is not scoped to code lines — it matches `//` and `///` comments. A
regression that replaces all real call sites with a local predicate
while leaving the doc comments mentioning `geometry::is_touchbar_digitizer`
untouched would PASS the invariant. The other guards in the same script
(#1, #2, #5, #6) DO scope to code lines via `grep -vE '^[0-9]+:\s*//'`;
guard #7 omits this filter. This is the same class of lesson as
ADR-031/NF-5 (grep guards must be code-scoped or they are theatrical).

ADR PROPOSAL D-031-2: scope guard #7a to code lines (exclude `//` and
`///` comments) so a comment-only mention does not satisfy the
single-source-of-truth invariant; OR strengthen to require ≥1 real CALL
site (e.g. grep for `is_touchbar_digitizer(` with a preceding non-comment
context). Logged, NOT implemented per FREEZE.

